{
 "fps": 30,
 "totalFrames": 1746,
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "He just dumped a hundred tons of lime into the Thames.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 74
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "And the river is about to send it back.",
   "from": 77,
   "to": 129
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "London, eighteen fifty-eight. Thirty degrees, and the heat won't break.",
   "from": 133,
   "to": 238
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "London's sewers empty into the river, right under Parliament's windows.",
   "from": 241,
   "to": 324
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Members flee their own library.",
   "from": 327,
   "to": 371
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "mp",
   "text": "Lime! Pour it into every sewer mouth!",
   "from": 374,
   "to": 436
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Barges tip lime at the sewer mouths, and the brown water slides away.",
   "from": 439,
   "to": 531
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "He throws open the window and breathes in.",
   "from": 535,
   "to": 576
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "mp",
   "text": "Gone! Good riddance, filthy river!",
   "from": 580,
   "to": 647
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "He flings his stinking hat after it.",
   "from": 651,
   "to": 690
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Then the tide turns.",
   "from": 693,
   "to": 739
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The river runs backward, and his hat floats right back.",
   "from": 755,
   "to": 848
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "With everything else. The committee runs for the door.",
   "from": 852,
   "to": 931
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Here's the catch. At Westminster, the Thames is tidal.",
   "from": 935,
   "to": 1018
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The sea pushes in, then drags out, over and over.",
   "from": 1022,
   "to": 1115
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Whatever you pour in sloshes up and down under your nose. Lime can't fix that.",
   "from": 1119,
   "to": 1240
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "So engineer Joseph Bazalgette catches the sewage before the river.",
   "from": 1244,
   "to": 1345
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Eighty-two miles of sewers carry it east, past the city.",
   "from": 1348,
   "to": 1421
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Into a reservoir holding twenty-seven million gallons.",
   "from": 1424,
   "to": 1498
  },
  {
   "i": 19,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The gates open at high tide, and the ebb drags it out to sea.",
   "from": 1502,
   "to": 1598
  },
  {
   "i": 20,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Parliament passed the law in just eighteen days.",
   "from": 1601,
   "to": 1660
  },
  {
   "i": 21,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "And the hat? It's still riding the tide.",
   "from": 1664,
   "to": 1722
  }
 ],
